# en-GB-oxendict: only the messages whose words differ from the house English (en-GB).
# Everything else falls back to English.

# Help text (i button) of the Blocking card.
settings-blocking-card-about = Uses HaGeZi's lists of adverts, trackers, and known bad sites, fetched once a day. While this is off, nothing runs. Name lookups go over an encrypted connection to the private server chosen here. Quad9 keeps no record of who asked. "Your network" still blocks, but is not private: your network's own servers see every lookup.

# Help text (i button) of the Firewall card.
settings-firewall-about = On, the firewall keeps out every connection from other computers that this computer did not ask for, so nobody on the same Wi-Fi can try their luck. Browsing, updates, and printers still work. A program that waits for others to connect, such as a game server, needs its port opened below. Off, every program that listens can be reached by any computer on the network. Switching it asks for the administrator's password.

